<title>UK: EIB ups 10-year bond to 750 billion lire.</title>
<headline>EIB ups 10-year bond to 750 billion lire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier by joint lead managers Banque Nationale de Paris, IMI Bank Luxembourg and San Paolo, has been increased to 750 billion lire from 500 billion lire.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    750 BLN ITL   COUPON     7.0	 MATURITY    12.FEB.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.532   PAY DATE    12.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA	 DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
